4115	3505	Digital and Group Bureaucracy and Mere Good Intentions. Moving further away from trust and attempting to get more in the way of honest inquiry and difficult interactions. Since  Our worst vice as a community is more of  a Common Cowardice, it is more of a passive aggressive as a reflection of the deeper insidious undermining of connection, achievement and fun that we see in society that we should be more afraid of.  \n\nIn the digital space historically this can be measured by at least 3 metrics, but there are more: (A) dwindling of engagement/participation on feeds and in crews. (B) disproportionate members showing up to subscribers (for instance a rise to 1,000 subscribers but a drop to 40 active engagers) (C) Increase in superficial postings, comments, and general drama. \n\nIf we continue to fail to create deeper bonds and further advantage our members through complimentary, coherent and directed efforts eventually our community will close by lack of these qualities.  Right now we continue with bureaucracy and lack of adequate vision, but this cannot sustain past the next 2 years. Estimated RIP without sufficient momentum toward deeper values in the community deliberately sought by a core grouping of 20 people at least. \n	\N	2023-11-08 03:51:36.700436	2023-11-13 16:09:25.577956	175	q7Py8ytsYCacbc4eRpzdgUR7	0
