o learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes, enthusiastically!	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:12.279053	2023-10-19 03:47:50.671473	\N	Daniel	McNichol	10899171	America/New_York	USA	7Fny3W2DTGgehjYd9b2dYtM4	1mcyqI_cmKdIcORYle361g	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
604	Naomi Veak	naomi@mysobergirlfriends.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/10955630	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=10955630	\N	2022-04-18 00:00:00	existing	Portland, OR	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\I do not. I saw this group mentioned in an article by Joe Lightfoot, linked from someone I know in the Authentic Relating community.  -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I've started a social community of sober women here in Portland, Oregon, and at 50 members I can already tell that I want to set up a structure that will support the sense of belonging and growth that includes smaller subsets, or pods. As an emerging community leader, I would like to learn more about community structure by participating in one like this.  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I am deeply immersed in Authentic Relating practices, shadow work, creativity, storytelling, intuition practices... I would love to have a space where I can talk about, share, and hear what others have to say on a variety of topics I'm interested in since I haven't been able to find many folks IRL to do that with. I'd also love to have a place to test out some of my ideas.  -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory 1.5  B) G