148	Anders Lund	anders.lund.work@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/12923253	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=12923253	2022-09-23 04:29:00	2022-09-22 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	Central Denmark Region, Denmark	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Perhaps - I hope so! -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Rebel Wisdom has been an epiphany to me. I have longed for a community for open and caring conversations about the big questions all my life. I found just that in Rebel Wisdom, and I am mourning losing it again. I am hoping EC could prove a home for the next step on my own journey to understand who I am (and who we are). -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I am curious by nature and drawn to a variety of topics. One topic that I would like to bring to the table is, what I believe to be, a narcissistic spiral that is currently unfolding in society. I am curious on this topic for many reasons; as a father to two little girls that appear to be growing up in a world with increasing deep narcissistic wounds. But also as a professional, where I work as a strategy advisor for large corporations - where the exact same spiral seems to be unfolding.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 2,5\nB) 2\nC) 3\nD) 3,5\nE) 3\nF) 2 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes!!	\N	\N	2022-11-25 06:57:19.508036	2023-10-19 03:47:51.344751	\N	Anders	Lund	12923253	Europe/Copenhagen	DNK	uzZp1kW7FKneovPe152QBi2j	HZcX5PkDX0Q534IVWm6j6g	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
924	David Martin	tweetings@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/19810238	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=19810238	2023-10-30 16:11:00	2023-11-07 11:30:24.6753	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	We invite you to a 1:1 Zoom Greeting call before admission to Emergent Commons.  Please check the e-mail you used for a message titled “Greetings from Emergent Commons” to schedule a greeting.  Do you know a current member?  If so, thank you for sharing their full name.\n\\I don’t know a current member.  -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\A hunger to find a community through which to better understand the world we are living in and the challenges of the day.  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I’m a psychotherapist and a trainee somatic therapist. I’m experienced in trauma and burnout and spiritual crisis – and the emergence that comes through crisis and difficulty. Also in recovery for deep burnout and trauma myself I’m developing new forms and protocols to help people renter the healthy flow of life. I’m interested in offering collaborative talks and workshops around what I know, for both those suffering and for the betterment of the well.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 1 \nB) 1 \nC) 4\nD) 4 \nE) 5 \nF) 5  -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes this sounds healthy and a good basis for the kind of discussions I want to have. 	First e-mail sent - Zoom done - Accepted	\N	2023-10-30 16:30:23.0419	2023-11-07 11:30:24.675886	2023-11-07 10:00:00	David	Martin	19810238	\N	\N	388r8sTHeEkYRrxSY3MiJ5Qs	\N	2023-10-30 19:50:45 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Esperanza V. Rodriguez\n2023-10-30 19:54:13 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> First e-mail sent - \n2023-10-31 21:31:49 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- when_timestamp changed: (blank) -> 2023-11-07 10:00:00 UTC\n2023-11-07 11:11:56 UTC\n- Join approval requested by Esperanza V. Rodriguez\n2023-11-07 11:15:08 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- notes changed: First e-mail sent -  -> First e-mail sent - Zoom done - Accepted\n	616	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
