362	Daniel Kidby	d.f.p.kidby@outlook.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/7786570	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=7786570	\N	2021-06-24 00:00:00	existing	Lancaster, United Kingdom	\N	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:06.15275	2023-10-19 03:47:48.66941	\N	Daniel	Kidby	7786570	Europe/London	GBR	nR8RNoAP8EHbXD53hX9g3hdD	kmDukArzxcvTstiJzH06Yw	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
61	Alex Poulin	alexandre.poulin12@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/13623541	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=13623541	2022-11-16 19:27:00	2022-11-16 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	Lake Brome, Canada	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\No, I do not. I would like to get to know people here.  -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\It was my desire to be part of a community. Not just any community. One is predicated on improving sensemaking and tackling this crisis. My hope is that as a collective, we will create initiatives addressing the crisis. Democracies -- and our global civilization -- need individuals to become enlightened if we stand a chance to mitigate global catastrophic and existential risks. The starting point is to make sense of these issues and our roles toward them.  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Exchanging ideas with others on the meta crisis. There is much for me to learn about the four-fold crisis and sensemaking is at the top of that list. However, I think I can bring unique perspectives and show other causes behind the meta crisis's generator functions. I want my thinking challenged and to challenge others. My aim is radical open-mindedness when receiving and giving ideas.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 3\nB) 2\nC) 2\nD) 3 \nE) 3\nF) 1 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\100% agree. And in this world of online communications, I will push myself to have video calls if conversations are too long. Our team at work is working to have more Zoom calls when written exchanges are too long. It avoids misinterpretation and contextualization. Care and honesty need to be at the forefront, which with our technology, can happen at a distance as long as we are willing to make the effort. 	\N	\N	2022-11-25 06:57:18.706336	2023-10-19 03:47:52.113235	\N	Alex	Poulin	13623541	America/Toronto	CAN	CgdSbQ42oSJ11X6EYibTHAZP	ksacrXBUUUPAltjlG4IXng	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	t
