g topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A 4\nB 3\nC 4\nD 2\nE 5\nF 4 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\100% agreed. I practice radical honesty with both my romantic and business partners as well as dialogue formats including 'navigating via tensions' from Sociocracy or 'clear-the-air' from NVC.\n\nI have daily weekly, monthly and annual reflection practices, and I long for a community who shares a similar ethos to shared inquiry; our internal struggles are all inter-connected...\n\n	\N	\N	2022-12-15 11:03:12.970632	2023-10-19 03:47:52.80543	\N	Marcus	Druen	14099881	\N	\N	CSJsE56xnbua1LuWAoBseGWK	qRL5PBicCEUF41hJdcYVjw	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	t
