131	Jeanny Gucher	jeanny@ourpatterns.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/13471288	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=13471288	2022-11-01 22:13:00	2022-11-01 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\My contact is my companion Teresa Zimmermann. -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\My first experience with Rebell Wisdom was in 2020, one of the interviews with Ken Wilber and instantly I felt a kind of homecoming experience.  There are people who seem to struggle or better who seem to love the same questions I was wondering about. Most exciting: the  variety of perspectives. So many different views, woven together  by these questions which resonate so deeply in myself. Hoping for more of that as direct conversation\n\n -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Through our initiative "our patterns" Teresa, Lene & myself are constantly creating integral, embodied content & tools and I'd love to share that ideas & questions with your community of pioneers in that fields. It's not so much about answers, is more about the process how we search for them through our own uncertainties, vulnerabilities & courageous moments.     -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory = 4 (love 