631	Maggie Barth	mbarth30@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/11758462	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=11758462	\N	2022-06-25 00:00:00	existing	St Louis Park, MN	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\I just met Ron during Collective Journaling with The Stoa. He shared the site with me. -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I work at a school with emergent curriculum. It's so beautiful. I could see this kind of community being something similar. I hope to experience both commonality and a respectful discord... a place to embrace each other and truly communicate and share, even if we do not agree. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I love education and learning. I have an aptitude for helping people find their gifts and strengths. I have recently discovered that I have strong somatic ("feeling sense") intuition and can articulate these experience well in the moment. -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A-1\nB-3\nC-4\nD-2\nE-4\nF-5 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves