633	Tim Banner	timbanner@mac.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/11774110	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=11774110	\N	2022-06-26 00:00:00	existing	Nelson Bay, Australia	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\Not sure but former participant with Rebel Wisdom -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\The Rebel Wisdom community was really great and enjoyable. I still feel that I'm moving toward a crossroads and would value access to a community that could help navigate that journey. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\My professional work envolves helping liberate organisations from being reductive and standardised when responding to human centred services. For the last 10 or so years I've been a critic. I feel at a crossroads with this work. What really lights me up is finding ways of moving from a critic to helping synthesis the different fears that hold people back. I'd love to share my experience of doing this. Specifically I've completed some writing that could form content.  -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A 2\nB 2\nC 4\nD 4\nE 2\nF 2 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. W