86	Douglas Prater	dvprater314@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/13620375	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=13620375	2022-11-12 04:09:00	2022-11-11 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	Atlanta, GA	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\I don't know anyone here personally, though I'm hoping to connect and meet others who are interested in the larger meta-project. -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\With the closing of Rebel Wisdom, I'm looking for a community with which I can engage in dialogue and practice. There's a lot of work to be done, and I hope to connect with others and do the aforementioned "work"- both on myself and in the world".  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\My speciality is "practice". I'm deeply engaged with the ideas of Integral theory, meta-modernism, and more, and it is my goal and my hope to bring the ideas to life through practice. I have a long history with medtitation practice from several traditions, and much of my work these days focuses on bringing the insights and practices of the integral model to the space of addiction recovery, addressing the problem practically and from all its inter-related dimensions. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory  -- 5\nB) Game B  -- 3\nC) Sensemaking  -- 3\nD) Complexity Theory -- 2, but very interested in learning more\nE) Meditation -- 5\nF) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing --2, but very VERY interested -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Absolutely yes, and I'm very much looking forward to connecting with a community whose members interact in this way.	\N	\N	2022-11-25 06:57:18.86202	2023-10-19 03:47:51.924008	\N	Douglas	Prater	13620375	America/Indiana/Indianapolis	USA	BNsuY8F8zwLWWLL4Zidw25Vm	wTeVAZqlOREGkJt5k8q0ww	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
182	Christian Beeck	christian.beeck@posteo.de	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/13823326	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=13823326	2022-11-26 13:42:00	2022-11-26 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\I've recently met a few people on the Last Campfire in London, as well as through the Collective Sensemaking calls. I don't know anybody on a more personal level, so wouldn't be comfortable to name them here. I hope you can understand this. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\When I did my first inqiury session on the RW sensemaking 101 course in 21, I was deeply moved of the connections arising in a virtual space when people share in openness and vulnerability. Back then, I was still dangling from the fingertips of a different group. So I needed time to fully disentangle, settle and see what's out there. I feel ready now and in essence I hope to offer my individual perspectives and vibrations to the community and hope to see completely unexpected things emerge. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I'm working on my "ecology of practices" (for me currently that's Zen meditation, Karate, breathwork and reading whenever I have the time) I'm very grateful for John Vervaeke's framework, since it truly helped me to make sense of what I was doing anyways. I'm no adept at any of the things I do, but sometimes even just sharing experiences among peers can be helpful. So I would see myself starting or joining a collective endeavor to support each other in building one's ecology of practices.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A3 / B2 / C3 / D1 / E4 / F3 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes.	kim nisbet\nLives in Berlin\n\n	\N	2022-11-26 14:14:39.017878	2023-10-19 03:47:52.645213	2022-11-29 17:00:00	Christian	Beeck	13823326	\N	\N	3uViF716QsFjrt3aZncFso7b	-LfDTV3bvMbxa-r9tJH16Q	2023-01-06 23:13:51 UTC by Kimberly Lathrop:\n- greeter_id changed: (blank) -> Kimberly Lathrop\n	215	\N	t	\N	\N	f
