800	David Nygaard	nygaard29@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/15538114	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=15538114	2023-03-12 23:19:00	2023-03-13 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Kimberly Lathrop  -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I got a green light after hearing about it from Kimberly. In my judgement its becoming a fragmented and polarized country and world. I am conflicted by it and spend a lot of bandwidth staying in the struggle struggle. I listen to the same podcasters and stay in an echo chamber of self affirming and growing distrust. Our institutions are broken. I am distrustful Iwant to breed more self peace of mind. I don't want to be in any fight. I need help in finding a middle ground and folks that can help  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I'm open . I have a full plate now and am acutely aware of over committing. I can see myself plugging into teams or pods that want to generate energy and content. I work much better collaboratively. I am and want to be a leader and also know I operate better creatively with people\nI'd have juice about trauma and unwinding how society is traumatizing and can recreate childhood trauma. I really enjoyed Gabor Mate's new book The myth of normal. I identify with how society can be toxic for meintegra -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\Integral 2 or 3\nGame b 1\nSense making 1 or 2\nComplexity theory 1\nMeditation 5\nWe space 4 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Absolutely. I will explore how my intentions may conflict with my impact on people. I also want to be humble while avoiding being self deprecating in my imperfection 	\N	\N	2023-03-12 23:42:02.632027	2023-10-19 03:47:53.280875	2023-03-19 12:00:00	David	Nygaard	15538114	\N	\N	gAxJ2YD1ZKvp1p51VQNzH8P4	\N	2023-03-13 01:49:19 UTC by Bryan Winchell:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Bryan Winchell\n2023-03-13 01:49:33 UTC\n- Join request approved by Bryan Winchell\n2023-03-14 23:39:01 UTC by Bryan Winchell:\n- when_timestamp changed: (blank) -> 2023-03-19 12:00:00 UTC\n	671	\N	t	\N	\N	f
