701	Joe Culhane	joseph.m.culhane@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/14606426	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=14606426	2023-01-15 19:04:00	2023-01-15 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Grace (Rebecca Rachmany), Hannah Close -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I am drawn into human communities who are working towards becoming more relational beings. I have a personal devotion to living this way and am always pleased to find others who are in an ongoing process of nature integration,  and practicing forms of engaged, embodied ecology, loving and loving with their more (and greater) than human communities. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I have many ideas to share, offer, and collaborate on. One being the work I’m co-creating around Relational Being, specifically practices and processes to create Ecological Selfies (similar to my profile pic), and other various content creation using embodied techniques building relationships with our shared ecology. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 4 \nB) 4\nC) 5\nD) 5\nE) 5\n5) 4 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Absolutely. Thank you for living in the ‘not knowing’ in this way with a pedagogy/ethics of care 🙏💞	interesting guy think he will fit right in \n\n	\N	2023-01-15 20:00:28.57525	2023-10-19 03:47:52.960651	2023-01-17 17:30:00	Joe	Culhane	14606426	\N	\N	rHieWgMAx64UuaGTw6LeDhQL	6zXxrtP_aiVZh9ILFd5PaQ	2023-01-15 20:33:24 UTC by damien maguire:\n- status changed: Pending -> 1st Email Sent\n2023-01-15 20:36:08 UTC\n- Join request approved by damien maguire\n2023-01-15 20:36:21 UTC by damien maguire:\n- status changed: Joined! -> 1st Email Sent\n2023-01-16 08:07:59 UTC by damien maguire:\n- status changed: 1st Email Sent -> Greet Scheduled\n2023-01-16 08:08:04 UTC by damien maguire:\n- when_timestamp changed: (blank) -> 2023-01-20T00:00:00.000Z\n2023-01-16 08:08:10 UTC by damien maguire:\n- when_timestamp changed: 2023-01-20 00:00:00 UTC -> 2023-01-20T16:00:00.000Z\n2023-01-16 08:08:16 UTC by damien maguire:\n- when_timestamp changed: 2023-01-20 16:00:00 UTC -> 2023-01-20T16:30:00.000Z\n2023-01-16 11:37:00 UTC by damien maguire:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> Could some\n2023-01-16 11:37:02 UTC by damien maguire:\n- notes changed: Could some -> Could someone \n2023-01-16 11:37:08 UTC by damien maguire:\n- notes changed: Could someone  -> Could someone help\n2023-01-16 11:37:11 UTC by damien maguire:\n- notes changed: Could someone help -> Could someone\n2023-01-16 11:37:12 UTC by damien maguire:\n- notes changed: Could someone -> Could someone \