665	Sherwin Yawn	yoy424051@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/14219653	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=14219653	2022-12-29 19:02:00	2022-12-29 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Nope -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I have always struggled to relate with other people. As I grew, I found that growing this connection and getting to know others are really fulfilling, but I feel like I am stuck. I listened to you guys' podcast with Stoa. It was really inspiring. I want to experience it. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I am in my last year of highschool, and I always feel like something is missing. It might just be my school, but most of the subjects are too focused on rote learning. There is a subject called Understanding Culture, but really, the teacher only let's us memorise terms and people. From what I have found, to understand something, you need to experience it. Books can only do so much. It is so easy to live with all of these ideas. It is only until I expressed them that I realized how bad they are. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A. 1 \nB. 1 \nC. 2\nD. 1\nE. 4\nF. 2 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes, I found this to be missing in schools. Teachers are disconnected with the experience of educating the students. Problems that pop up are rarely solved except when the parents of students are willing to spend their time to strike a complaint. There isn't this feedback loop. There's no "connection." It causes schools to be stagnant and not improve. I want to see if it really works because maybe just maybe, it doesn't work.	Sherwin's a really nice guy and has been asking me several questions via DM seeking to get involved.	\N	2022-12-30 04:43:53.302378	2023-10-19 03:47:52.853144	2023-01-15 08:00:00	Sherwin	Yawn	14219653	\N	\N	HCwqGvX88uFyTwA8ZpD3sWXa	N5Z_OCAMNsLRJJqqUvPcyg	2023-01-05 14:57:26 UTC by John Stokdijk:\n- status changed: 1st Email Sent -> Completed\n2023-01-05 20:08:42 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- status changed: Completed -> 2nd Email Sent\n2023-01-08 06:00:22 UTC by Bryan Winchell:\n- greeter_id changed: (blank) -> Bryan Winchell\n2023-01-09 03:34:35 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- greeter_id changed: 671 -> Kevin Triplett\n2023-01-09 03:34:36 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- greeter_id changed: 329 -> Kevin Triplett\n2023-01-09 20:05:48 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- greeter changed: Kevin Triplett -> (blank)\n2023-01-11 11:33:44 UTC by Bryan Winchell:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Bryan Winchell\n2023-01-11 11:33:57 UTC by Bryan Winchell:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> John S. a