939	Frieda-Raye Green	friedarayegreen@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/21302317	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=21302317	2024-01-13 00:41:00	2024-02-20 16:50:36.917911	Scheduling Zoom	\N	We invite you to a 1:1 Zoom Greeting call before admission to Emergent Commons.  Please check the e-mail you used for a message titled “Greetings from Emergent Commons” to schedule a greeting.  Do you know a current member?  If so, thank you for sharing their full name.\n\\I learned about emergent commons from someone in James Baker's  Intentional Society, where I am a new member. I dont recall his name, I am still new. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I am interested in deepening learning relationally, and in deepening my relationships in general. I am exploring communities that center intersubjectivity. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I am an installation artist, yoga teacher and creative thinker, currently doing a second undergrad in cognitive systems with a focus on philosophy of mind. I am considering eventually moving into the somatic therapy world. What is central in my thinking, acting and feeling right now is a desire for deeper community connection. Intersubjectivity as a spiritual path. I want more opportunity to practice designing and creating things in community.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 3 B) 2 C)3 D) 3 E) 4 F) 3 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\absolutely.	\N	\N	2024-01-13 01:00:31.956468	2024-02-20 16:50:36.918647	\N	Frieda-Raye	Green	21302317	\N	\N	rAfEerRMLU7MoD86NDvBXour	\N	2024-01-13 22:50:34 UTC by Derick Galea:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Derick Galea\n2024-02-20 16:46:11 UTC\n- Join approval requested by Derick Galea\n	446	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
