590	Brad Sayers	bradsayers@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/10412860	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=10412860	\N	2022-03-02 00:00:00	existing	Warwick, Canada	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\I do not. -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I follow lots of people related to the so called liminal web -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Well, I know that we are in a paradigm shift to who knows what....I like to believe that by majoring on the majors and minoring on the minors (ie, living according to periennal core values of human dignity and potential) we can continue here on this amazing planet -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory - 4\nB) Game B - 1\nC) Sensemaking - 3\nD) Complex Theory - 0 \nE) Meditation -3.5\nF) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing - .5 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes, these are also my practices	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:12.137942	2023-10-19 03:47:50.566724	\N	Brad	Sayers	10412860	America/Toronto	CAN	iiPAZaV3rJvx2JHceGVBCrfE	Xmh7FrColgVymhZc2DL2iA	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
149	Martti Lemieux	martti@pentomic.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/12901503	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=12901503	2022-09-21 20:26:00	2022-09-21 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	Sault Ste Marie, Canada	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\I don't personally know Matt Habermehl, but it was through a link he posted on the Consciousness & Conscience Discord server that I learned of the EC. -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\The idea of people working to come into right relation with both themselves and the world is what attracted me. Sense-making, tool-making, and sharing are what I hope to experience.  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Tools to better navigate the world light me up. As a product and communication designer, I enjoy building tools for applied sense-making. Sometimes it's simply translating abstract concepts into plain language, mapping systems, or developing cognitive interfaces to better interact with the world. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory = 2\nB) Game B = 1\nC) Sensemaking = 5\nD) Complexity Theory =1\nE) Meditation = 3\nF) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing = 5 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\I do.	\N	\N	2022-11-25 06:57:19.520689	2023-10-19 03:47:51.333613	\N	Martti	Lemieux	12901503	America/Toronto	CAN	5oKpTZQsprYzkSTn8pRrnXT7	k5iWU8aUe1AehU-N05-G3g	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
