573	Tiffany Elsener	tiffany.elsener@me.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/9966519	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=9966519	\N	2022-01-24 00:00:00	existing	North Vancouver District, Canada	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\no. I found this from a Perspectiva event\n\n -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Since completing my thesis on integral and metamodern approaches to leadership, I've been seeking further community to drive knowledge to action while also be present to emergence and the collective. I'm hoping to experience deeper discussion with fellow humans and supporting each other as we co-create new perspectives and holistic approaches to our current crises. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Co-creation and intra-action are both terms that I've been exploring and embodying in the last few years. As well, I've participated in education from DAOs (decentralized autonomous organizations), and there is huge wisdom in the collective and reframing leadership and action as intersubjective experiences. I feel there is so much power in the collective imagination and discourse enabled by the ability to communicate over space and time through technology. \n -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory 5\nB) Game B 2\nC) Sensemaking 3\nD) Complex Theory 3\nE) Meditation 4\nF) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing 3 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\I got goosebumps reading this sub-section, as this approach to relating feels so resonant, yet I crave it. Yes! I agree to join and relate in this space as outlined.	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:11.9625	2023-10-19 03:47:50.428498	\N	Tiffany	Elsener	9966519	America/Vancouver	CAN	gjvhu4CgC1WJWd5NwwCWoxTr	RVdDBtNmQFOGFir-rmOlWQ	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
589	Afam Okoh	afamokoh@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/10406324	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=10406324	\N	2022-03-02 00:00:00	existing	London, United Kingdom	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\James Baker, Jochen Weber -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I've joined Intentional Society and am looking to experience more communities that are trying new methods of relating to each other. Also communities that encourage adult development/ flourishing. I am looking to contribute, learn from and be in dynamic and healthy relation to others. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I have several strong interests including meditation, crypto communities and thinking about practices that allow one to experience different models of the world. When it comes to sharing I tend to take my time getting to understand the contours of a community and how much I want to engage then decide on how to share appropriate to that context. -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\\nA) 2 - listened to a couple of Ken Wilbur podcast and read some blogs on spiral dynamics\nB) 4 - read most of the key works is how I got interested in this space.\nC) 2 - understand intellectually not really done in practice\nD) 2 - have a basic intellectual understanding and an interest in learning more but do not have a strong experential/ practical understanding.\nE) 3 - meditate between 1 - 2 hours daily but still at an early stage in my path compared to any experienced teachers.\nF) 3  -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:12.127871	2023-10-19 03:47:50.55908	\N	Afam	Okoh	10406324	Europe/London	GBR	7Xnpw4yZytQ8wyT9Jvc1MPY5	y5poU7Op9JoV-1pyZuXBYQ	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
