655	Mason Green	shift.think@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/12064983	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=12064983	\N	2022-07-21 00:00:00	existing	Portland, OR	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\I am not sure if I do, but I'm not sure. You don't know what you don't know ;) -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Heard about it via a Twitter post, when I found the group the description was intriguing and I had already known a lot about RW's work so it seemed great.\n\nI hope to connect with others in meaningful and authentic ways on a variety of topics. I don't have a ton of people I can talk to about topics related to RW and I imagine this space would allow for that. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\The idea of exploring new and emerging ways of living, organizing and running society is what I think about regularly.  Much of what RW discusses has fed into these ideas for me and it's here where I'd like to explore what others have to say and contribute as well. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 2\nB) 4\nC) 5\nD) 3\nE) 4\nF) 3 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes.	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:13.058511	2023-10-19 03:47:51.100645	\N	Mason	Green	12064983	America/Toronto	USA	XByaZkfbh1gifmowSyFhp1fU	i5ScyqoqxHdFjX3_C1WVQQ	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
639	Zsolt Tanko	zsolttanko@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/11879301	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=11879301	\N	2022-07-05 00:00:00	existing	Ottawa, Canada	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\Ron Walkow -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Long time follower of Rebel Wisdom and the Stoa looking to join an active community of like-minded folks. Mostly looking for dialogos - I've passively absorbed enough content, time to engage others! -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\My background is in the pragmatic dharma scene, where I went pretty deep into meditation and awakening stuff for a few years. My particular path - the dharma being preceded by a phd in math - has afforded what appears to be a unique view on some things. Maybe this'll be a relevant venue to share some of it. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 3\nB) 3\nC) 5\nD) 4\nE) 5\nF) 3 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yup.	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:12.799471	2023-10-19 03:47:50.951206	\N	Zsolt	Tanko	11879301	America/Toronto	CAN	FfXtigGQeREFcJdLbjVMrq39	agX7h8LbZvwKn4gM7URHLw	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
