653	David Swedlow	dls78731@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/12051476	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=12051476	\N	2022-07-20 00:00:00	existing	Austin, TX	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\Tucker Walsh -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Harvesting after the Austin Emerge gathering -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Practices and spaces for maturing collective wisdom and rewilding homo sapiens to awaken living as gaia. This involves deep life-based alchemy that heals individual and collective wounding. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 4.5\nB) 4\nC) 5\nD) 4\nE) 3\nF) 5+ -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\With joy! This powerful evolutionary alchemical moment, including massive individual and civilizational transformation requires the most wide compassion humans have ever needed to muster on a huge scale. Egos will be bruised and broken at all scales to birth new structures of consciousness we can't even imagine currently. I'm keen to help cultivate the practices and policies that help us through the transition, and have little egoic affiliation/attachment with any specific "side"	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:13.039154	2023-10-19 03:47:51.084789	\N	David	Swedlow	12051476	America/Chicago	USA	Wu1kD5QWLs3Jaik49LmmYfaB	OTg279EoSNLRe0f_6_IYQQ	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
654	Judi Neal	judi@edgewalkers.org	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/12052399	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=12052399	\N	2022-07-20 00:00:00	existing	Fayetteville, AR	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\Tomas Bjorkman, Erik Muten -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I am the executive director of The Global Consciousness Institute, with a goal of legitimizing the study of global consciousness in higher education. I come here to learn about what others are doing and to partner. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I get lit up by work on practical spirituality and how that can scale globally. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A. 3\nB. 2\nC. 1\nD. 3\nE. 4\nF. 2\n -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes. This is part of what attracts me. I was at Emerge Austin and honor the openness and consciousness of this community.	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:13.048671	2023-10-19 03:47:51.092707	\N	Judi	Neal	12052399		USA	QwqgySxo6HY5T2Xad1Xw52Xr	tkjIIghjeztvlzJ6D94_yg	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
571	Leonie Cooper	cooper.leoniejoy@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/9954946	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=9954946	\N	2022-01-24 00:00:00	existing	Melbourne, Australia	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their name!\n\\Monika Bravo -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\A few years ago, I was trying to put some of what was emerging around the commons into community 'work'. I've fallen out of touch with it - so much has emerged (which is exciting). I am a para-academic who has and remains critical of the institution and is seeking communites where knowledge is enacted/practised and shared. I'm choosing this community as an act of reaching out and a promise to find and support others. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Wow. This question makes me want to be part of this community. To be honest, I don't know 'til I'm there because, for me, the answer is "people". What is their spark? I orienate towards processes, methods. The "how-tos". How do we move from 'ideas' to actions? From thought to matter  - and matter to thought.  Philoshopy; art; writing: as practices might offer a (rather broad) start. :) -:- The following list shows some of the interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complex Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\integral theory - 2\nGame B - 1\nComplex Theory - 2\nMediation - 3\nWe-space practices - 2 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes. You say this beautifully as a demonstration of this practice of care and honesty in relating. Thank you.	\N	\N	2022-12-11 08:05:11.936673	2023-10-19 03:47:50.412621	\N	Leonie	Cooper	9954946	Australia/Sydney	AUS	HoT6NapU822otcbJ9uvVCaSG	s7c7iqkCG0iYO9nN2aD5RA	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
