900	Christian Swenson	christian.swenson@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/18621249	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=18621249	2023-09-04 17:17:00	2023-09-06 00:00:00	No Response (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\I'm very good friend with Sondra Charbadze. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Sondra recommended it. I am particularly interested in the subgroup "way beyond naturalism." I would like to contribute to an ongoing conversation about the limitations of naturalism, the failings of materialism, and ways to look beyond them to deeper and higher realities. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I am deeply invested in spiritual teachers past and present who bring a more empirical approach to their teachings. Emanuel Swedenborg and Rudolf Steiner are two big cases in point for me. I am well versed in both of their spiritual systems. I have published and given conference presentations about both. Moreover, I am deeply interested in contemporary accounts of higher realities like NDEs or psychedelics trip reports. I am good synthesis and good at uncovering patterns and connections. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A: 2, B: 3, C: 2, D: 2, E: 5, F: 1 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\I absolutely agree to do this.	\N	\N	2023-09-04 17:30:44.174972	2023-10-23 20:04:55.935734	\N	Christian	Swenson	18621249	\N	\N	EeLHZSq1YYtrBNt3Bwj5wYWz	\N	2023-09-06 19:41:09 UTC\n- Join approval requested by Derick Galea\n	446	\N	t	\N	\N	f
821	Noah Boardman	noah.boardman@protonmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/16310806	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=16310806	2023-04-27 05:05:00	2023-05-02 00:00:00	Chat Done (completed)	\N	We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I am lit up by active grass-roots movements working to enrich our shared ecosystems (social, cultural, natural) in direct, practical ways that can be shared, joined, copied and tweaked. Discussions of philosophies of action are always enjoyable. I love (human) arts, culture, literature, music. I hope to share in this by Finding The Others, learning as much as I can from them and teaching what I can while putting the ideas generated in this space into some form of practice. -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\You have my word -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I discovered Emergent Commons during the last Rebel Wisdom event, a space which was more meaningful to me than I realized at the time. I was drawn here by the concept of a grass-roots branching/continuation of RW, especially the relational work. I am hoping to find a place of real i