823	Julian Filice	julian.filice@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/16443959	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=16443959	2023-05-04 19:35:00	2023-05-04 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Other than those I met today at a Stoa crossover event (Fanny Norlin), no. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I was drawn by a very engaging and beautiful event that led to invitations to collaborate with a few EC members in the space on new ideas that feel really powerful and valuable. I hope to experience an environment to foster connection, grow together, improve our skill at relating to self and others, learn and expand my mind :) -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Wow, it's hard to even know how to start. A few topics came up today that seemed to have potential to be very powerful. 1) A "Panic Room" - loosely envisioned as a place to explore and express our deep fears in a group setting where one can feel held, supported and empowered to withstand intensity that might feel intimidating or overwhelming alone. 2) Spaces where participants of one gender offer only witnessing and support to the other to encourage the exploration of femininity and masculinity. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 2\nB) 4\nC) 4\nD) 1\nE) 4\nF) 5 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Absolutely. Sounds like a wonderful summary of healthy communion.	Attended The Stoa Embassy event	\N	2023-05-04 19:41:10.272881	2023-10-19 03:47:53.435089	\N	Julian	Filice	16443959	\N	\N	6W5y135pxUc1Wc6yQvKSATaP	\N	2023-05-08 15:49:22 UTC by mari budlong:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> mari budlong\n2023-05-10 17:49:26 UTC by mari budlong:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> Attended The Stoa Embassy event\n	207	\N	t	\N	\N	t
