115	Jamie Johnstone	johnstone00jamie@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/13553971	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=13553971	2022-11-07 19:07:00	2022-11-07 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom		Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Not that I am aware of.  -:- What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I've participated in Sense-making 101 courses, followed there conversations and recently attended their final event. \n\nWhat initially drew me to this community was the a broad range of themes that I could sense intuitively as needed and missing from many other contemporary discourse and culture. \n\nI hope to experience connection and a sense of growth and growing together.  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I'm really drawn to John Vervakes idea  of an ecology of practice. I'm curious about how developmental paths (of EOPs) can be designed and include individual and collective manifestations. \n\nI'm interested in cultivating wisdom, sensemaking and thinking clearly and community that support each other; provide checks and balances in this process.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 2\nB) 2 \nC) 3 \nD) 2\nE) 4\nF) 2 \n -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Developing this capacity is a huge part of my interest in joining this community. \n\nQuestioning my own beliefs and my capacity to be in relationship as a project has shown its significance and urgency in my response to experience's of 'spiritual emergency' (10 Years ago). I continue to learn a lot from the integration process from these experiences. 	\N	\N	2022-11-25 06:57:19.133961	2023-10-19 03:47:51.622295	\N	Jamie	Johnstone	13553971	Europe/London	\N	EN7Hw14CLT9hSyHkJa8RrNaE	TgAaQNj4kSMdSzq19Ljqrw	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	f
