813	Daniel Haeberlé	dhaeberle@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/16004217	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=16004217	2023-04-08 12:29:00	2023-04-11 00:00:00	Scheduling Zoom	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Ivo Mensch\nGeorge Por -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\Was member of Rebel Wisdom for its last year. Met a lot of members at  November 2022 London closing event who told me I should be here given my passion for societal change through better sense-making. I hope to experience the same feeling of belonging - kindred souls - I experienced at RW events, and to find others I can further grow with and initiate projects with. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I've been  strongly called to facilitating transformative learning at the individual and collective levels. Tired of feeling isolated, I want to join others in explorative conversation and action with to help midwife the epistemological readjustment our societies are in the throes of. Forms of contribution can range from respectfully listening, presencing and witnessing, to contributing my voice, or to co-designing and facilitating innovative learning events or media. I am open to what emerges. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory    3\nB) Game B  2\nC) Sensemaking   4\nD) Complexity Theory  4\nE) Meditation  3\nF) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing  4\n\n -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes I Agree. This culture is what I seek and commit to upholding.	email sent \n	\N	2023-04-08 12:30:48.162523	2023-10-19 03:47:53.370778	\N	Daniel	Haeberlé	16004217	\N	\N	UoUFM4Qca5g6fHmHbuzJwFsr	\N	2023-04-11 17:27:10 UTC\n- Join request approved by Fahiym Hanna\n2023-04-12 15:10:26 UTC by Fahiym Hanna:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> email sent \n\n	556	\N	t	\N	\N	t
