838	Tim Noppeney	tim.noppeney@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/13783918	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=13783918	2023-05-27 09:15:00	2023-05-29 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Patrick Wentrop  -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I want to connect with like-minded people who are working on creating solutions for a better world. The more we surround ourselves with inspiring people and support each other, the more true value we can create for others. I also want to meet people who are very different from myself yet driven by similar values so that I can open myself up to new worlds.  -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I'm deeply fascinated by building relationships and consciously developing as a human being which is what I want to bring into people's life. Especially the idea of building systems that make truly intimate relationships the norm excites me. No matter whether this is on an individual or collective level. I believe that my knowledge and skills in this field as well as my desire to giving gifts with kindness will in one way or another contribute to the lives of the people in this community.  -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A2, B3, C3, D1, E3, F2 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Most definitely! I live by core principles of radical honesty, kind compassion & fairness and a love of learning & curiosity. So I'm looking forward to engaging in a cummity full of trust so that we can vulnerably relate to one another and this way grow together. 	First e-mail sent 29may - scheduling zoom - taking over for Esperanza at her request	\N	2023-05-27 09:20:59.882553	2024-01-01 05:46:20.555683	\N	Tim	Noppeney	13783918	\N	\N	4Qgcipqjwj1oZYmYox1k6KUE	\N	2023-05-29 13:55:07 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Esperanza V. Rodriguez\n2023-05-29 13:57:33 UTC\n- Join approval requested by Esperanza V. Rodriguez\n2023-05-29 14:07:08 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> First e-mail sent 29may -\n2023-06-04 09:24:31 UTC by Esperanza V. Rodriguez:\n- notes changed: First e-mail sent 29may - -> First e-mail sent 29may - scheduling zoom\n2023-06-05 15:13:12 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- greeter changed: 616 -> Kevin Triplett\n2023-06-05 15:13:59 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- notes changed: First e-mail sent 29may - scheduling zoom -> First e-mail sent 29may - scheduling zoom - taking over for Esperanza at her request\n	329	\N	t	\N	\N	t
