912	Joshua Nelson	josh@affekttraining.com	\N	\N	2023-09-26 23:11:00	\N	Pending	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Personally, no. I have followed the work of Peter for several months now. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I'm not sure... instinctually I might say ideas... the breaking down of philosophical boundaries, but I'm not entirely sure that is it.\n\nSelf-creation, self-improvement perhaps. If I had to put into words, it may be something like de-creation (yes, Weil), but also Japanese art. De-creation is described as "to design a mechanism to summon the future." I think this aptly described my situation - to train my sensibility towards de-creation. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I love philosophy. I have never studied it academically. I dropped out of high school, after which I studied holistic health etc, I now own a gym called Affekt.\nTo say we're not a "regular" gym would be proverbial. That being said I take an approach to training that is marred in philosophical dissent from the standard self-motivation tactics so highly sought and sold - I can't explain it which is maybe why I'm here. I want to cultivate a space of creativity, I've found much of that here. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 2\nB) 2\nC) 3\nD) 1\nE) 4/5\nF) 1 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Absolutely. I'm not sure what all of this will look like, but here's to touching that unseen, yet familiar surface (hyper-objects, Morton).	email sent to arrange zoom 27/9\nreminder sent 1/10	\N	2023-09-26 23:30:32.830471	2023-10-01 09:17:51.156812	\N	Joshua	Nelson	\N	\N	\N	yFft9PtE6Yn3eYreUgsnW1kE	\N	\n2023-09-27 13:37:03 UTC by Erik H:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> email sent to arrange zoom 27/9\n2023-09-27 13:37:14 UTC by Erik H:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Erik H\n2023-10-01 09:17:51 UTC by Erik H:\n- notes changed: email sent to arrange zoom 27/9 -> email sent to arrange zoom 27/9\nreminder sent 1/10\n	17	\N	f	\N	\N	\N
