854	Leslie Yeargers	leslie@yeargers.net	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/17557698	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=17557698	2023-07-09 20:17:00	2023-07-15 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Kalima Sawyer (Catheryn Sawyer) and Claudia Dommaschk -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I joined Rebel Wisdom rather late in its incarnation and took the last Sensemaking 101 class. I virtually attended Rebel Wisdom's final event and heard about Emergent Commons there. Both my pod members, Claudia and Kalima, joined and have encouraged me to join. I hope to experience more of the same relational sense making experience I received in Rebel Wisdom. I also hope to learn about different perspectives and engage in dialogue that supports expanding world views. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\What lights me up is the connection that happens when people participate in good faith dialogues around difficult, contentious and polarizing topics. As a mental health therapist focused on cognitive, emotional, spiritual and relational processes, I like being challenged and challenging others in a respectful, heartfelt, connective manner. Without experiencing EC first hand, it's hard to say all the ways in which I will get involved, but I believe I will find an inroad into the community. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a 