918	Ladaun Jackson	ljackson86@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/19456632	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=19456632	2023-10-12 15:26:00	2023-10-17 03:54:30.471965	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Not sure -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I've participated in and led relational practices (Authentic Relating and Circling) in Austin, TX for almost 10 years.  Recent changes in the community structure have spurred me to look for alternative ways to connect with an even broader network of people involved in sensemaking, wisdom, heart-centered relating, etc.  Here, I hope to find like-minded people and connect to work together in ways that enrich our lives.   -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I'm lit up by searching for and finding ever deeper layers of truth.  My favorite way to enter a flow state is with conversation, so I have a project I stared locally that I'd like to bring here called, obviously, the Conversation Project - unmoderated (but governed by a set of mutually agreed upon principles) one-on-one real-time discussions on a provocative idea or subject area.     -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 5 \nB) 1\nC) 5\nD) 3\nE) 3\nF) 5 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\YES!	\N	\N	2023-10-12 15:30:24.083135	2023-10-19 03:54:51.63572	\N	Ladaun	Jackson	19456632	\N	\N	bSQZLyY68XUxaLsqT3ogGhp4	\N	2023-10-13 05:51:02 UTC by mari budlong:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> mari budlong\n	207	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
860	Don Salmon	donsalmon7@gmail.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/17952620	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=17952620	2023-07-31 15:32:00	2023-08-01 00:00:00	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	Do you know someone in this community?  If so, please share their full name.\n\\Kimberly Lathrop -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I've known Kimberly since we were in an integral study group 10 years ago.  Just the fact that someone as conscious, caring and compassionate as she is loves this group is enough in itself. \n\nI've been interested in the marriage of spirituality and social change for decades; among numerous things, I led the Compassionate Action Meditation group at the New York Open Center from 1992-95, and  a chapter in our book on Sri Aurobindo's yogic psychology focuses on the transformation of society. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\It is is wonderful to be among people who share a passion for supporting the emergence of the new integral consciousness.\n\nI have been writing, teaching and sharing on this since the 1970s, and continue to marvel at how much this emergence has hastened, radically intensified in just the last decade or so.\n\nI'll be delighted to share writing, speaking videos, music and more,  as a musician, clinical psychologist and long time contemplative.\n\nSee www.RememberToBe.Life for more. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 5 (I've written at length on how this relates to both Jean Gebser's and Sri Aurobindo's notion of "integral")\nB) 1\nC) 1\nD) 4\nE) 5 - Christian, Sufi, Zen, Integral (Sri Aurobindo), Tibetan Buddhism, among others\nF) 4 (see below on the practice of "Insight Dialogue") -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\relating this way is one of the main things that draws me to this community. Jan (my wife, and also member of the integral group where we met Kimberly) and I taught "Insight Dialog" for several years in New York, a practice developed by insight meditation teacher Greg Kramer of which the essence is making space to hear ourselves and one another, to listen from that vast spaciousness, of awareness, of the heart, of the earth.	\N	\N	2023-07-31 15:39:01.649218	2024-02-05 21:47:11.206564	\N	Don	Salmon	17952620	\N	\N	nUkjpJBsQ3SLzahoNYBynsgT	tUeYsgOvXL8_6aHxXRhLEw	2023-08-01 08:48:29 UTC\n- Join approval requested by Derick Galea\n	446	\N	t	\N	\N	f
