988	Atma A	atma_anand@outlook.com	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/30187722	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=30187722	2024-11-25 17:57:00	2024-11-30 20:50:23.524804	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	We invite you to a 1:1 Zoom Greeting call before admission to Emergent Commons.  Please check the e-mail you used for a message titled “Greetings from Emergent Commons” to schedule a greeting.  Do you know a current member?  If so, thank you for sharing their full name.\n\\I do not know any members. I was redirected here by Rebel Wisdom's last blog post. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I was looking for a group which goes beyond LessWrong and similar purely rational spaces after my multiple 7-day Zen Sesshins, and in-person philosophy meetups.\n\nIt is very hard to find people who think beyond meta-rationality. As a 29-year-old in the middle of wrapping up an Astrophysics PhD, the challenge to find people such people in-person is even harder. I do try to experience things without any preconceived notions, but not having an intent is confusion. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\Since the last 3 years I have been building up a multi-disciplinary approach to know the limits of understanding. However, I can only speak definitely about Physics and Zen - all of my other intermediate levels of complexity being from an Indian education system till undergrad, popular books, and webpages. I am currently exploring ways for community building and physical activities which promote it, and reading more books from interdisciplinary professors which I am happy to discuss about. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 3, B) 1, C) 2, D) 5, E) 5, F) 4 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes.	2024-11-28, email sent	\N	2024-11-25 18:00:27.330229	2024-11-30 20:50:23.525451	2024-11-30 05:00:00	Atma	A	30187722	\N	\N	1731mJwWaLSgz45W2H4ayH4F	\N	2024-11-28 23:02:15 UTC by AlekSasha Marino:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> AlekSasha Marino\n2024-11-28 23:16:32 UTC by AlekSasha Marino:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> 2024-11-28, email sent\n2024-11-30 19:46:51 UTC by AlekSasha Marino:\n- when_timestamp changed: (blank) -> 2024-11-30 05:00:00 UTC\n2024-11-30 20:45:32 UTC\n- Join approval requested by AlekSasha Marino\n	203	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
