h 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) Integral Theory - 3\nB) Game B - 2\nC) Sensemaking - 4\nD) Complexity Theory - 3\nE) Meditation - 4\nF) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating, and/or Collective Presencing - 3 -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes, I agree to join the community and relate in this way. I appreciate the focus on conscious communication, self-awareness, and open inquiry. I'm committed to engaging in thoughtful and respectful conversations, learning from others, and contributing to a space that fosters care, honesty, and growth.	\N	\N	2024-12-04 11:00:24.971246	2024-12-04 13:30:26.646742	\N	Indian	Renters	\N	\N	\N	MdzH4xne7JjvoMmAVnjVxCgU	\N	2024-12-04 13:30:26 UTC by AlekSasha Marino:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> AlekSasha Marino\n	203	\N	f	\N	\N	\N
