1004	Kim Sellberg	kim@lumeon.dev	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/members/33454020	https://emergent-commons.mn.co/chats/new?user_id=33454020	2025-04-24 17:08:00	2025-05-06 13:50:35.882632	Zoom Done (completed)	\N	We invite you to a 1:1 Zoom Greeting call before admission to Emergent Commons.  Please check the e-mail you used for a message titled “Greetings from Emergent Commons” to schedule a greeting.  Do you know a current member?  If so, thank you for sharing their full name.\n\\I don’t think I know anyone in the community yet. -:- Because a main focus in this community is relational in nature, we strongly encourage using real names-- at the very least a first name and last initial.  We also strongly encourage the use of real photos. What drew you to this community?  What do you hope to experience here?\n\\I came across this community through Rebel Wisdom, and based on that connection, I have a sense that this might be a community where I can meet kindred spirits, people open to sharing, learning, and co-creating together.\n\nI’m hoping to find meaningful connection, inspiration, and opportunities for collaboration. -:- We do not have an individual or a team creating, curating or broadcasting content.  It's our members that bring the content, create events, start groups and spark discussion.  What lights you up and how do you think you might share that here?\\I have experience with both online and local networks and communities, often within globally interconnected contexts. My work is closely tied to community building, coordination, and co-creation, so I believe I can bring a broad range of perspectives, resources and contributions.\n\nYour decentralized and autopoietic model represents the future of networks and human coordination, and it aligns closely with my overall philosophy. -:- The following list shows some interests of some members in this community.  To help us understand where our new members are starting out (this is not a test), please let us know which of the following topics you are familiar with by typing a number after each from 1 to 5, with 1= not familiar and 5= very familiar.  \nA) Integral Theory    B) Game B    C) Sensemaking    D) Complexity Theory   E) Meditation     F) We-Space practices like Circling, Authentic Relating and/or Collective Presencing\\A) 4 – My life shifted many years ago in a bookstore in Boulder, when I came across Wilber’s A Brief History of Everything.\n\nB) 3 – I was part of the Game B Discord a few years back, though I wasn’t very active.\n\nC) 3 – Rebel Wisdom and Daniel S introduced me to the dimension of sensemaking, which I now see as vital for the evolution of humanity.\n\nE) 4 – Systems thinking and complexity theory are deeply integrated into my everyday life/ perspective. I'm also part of the core team at Si Network. -:- We are dedicated to consciously communicating with care and honesty. We question our own beliefs, explore comfort in not knowing, and welcome shared inquiry. We are willing to have difficult conversations and make space to hear another. We check in with ourselves about our reactions and needs in conversation.  When we don't meet our standards we are committed to learning, improving and staying related.\nDo you agree to joining our community and relating in this way?\\Yes, I do! This is exactly what I’m looking for, and something I sense is, unfortunately, in short supply: a context that is open, authentic, and adaptive.\n\nI hope this resonates with the Emergent Commons community, and if it does, I’m really looking forward to connecting on the 1:1 greeting call.\n\nWarmest,\nKim Sellberg	1st email sent 2025/04/28	\N	2025-04-28 16:09:00.870912	2025-05-06 13:50:35.883456	\N	Kim	Sellberg	33454020	\N	\N	eRL82LiKK6uZm7Rnsw1ja2B8	\N	2025-04-28 16:12:52 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- greeter changed: (blank) -> Kevin Triplett\n2025-04-28 16:15:43 UTC by Kevin Triplett:\n- notes changed: (blank) -> 1st email sent 2025/04/28\n2025-05-06 13:49:47 UTC\n- Join approval 